    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does the EU BPR apply to disinfectants manufactured outside the EU?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. The EU BPR applies to any biocidal product placed on the EU market, regardless of where it was manufactured. A non-EU manufacturer selling into the EU must designate an EU-based Responsible Person — an individual or company established in the EU who accepts legal responsibility for the product's compliance with the BPR. The Responsible Person holds the product authorisation or is named as the authorisation holder's representative, and is the point of contact for EU competent authorities. Without an EU Responsible Person, the product cannot legally be sold in the EU. This is a critical structural requirement that many non-EU manufacturers underestimate when first approaching the EU market." }
