        File: eu-biocidal-products-regulation-disinfectants-sanitisers-diagram-globalformulation.webp
        Alt: EU biocidal products regulation authorisation pathway diagram — active substance approval, national authorisation, mutual recognition, and Union authorisation routes | Global Formulation
        IMG PROMPT (900×500px): Premium 3D scientific visualization. EU BPR authorisation pathway flowchart on a dark navy (#0a1628) background. Two parallel vertical columns flowing downward: left column shows active substance approval pathway — glowing cyan boxes for ECHA dossier submission, member state evaluation, Commission decision, and Union list inclusion; right column shows product authorisation pathway — gold boxes for national authorisation application, competent authority review, authorisation decision, then branching right to mutual recognition pathway and left to Union authorisation centralised route. Glowing cyan connecting arrows between the two columns at the active substance approval box linking to product authorisation entry. Clean sequential compliance pathway boxes with glowing connector lines. Regulatory authority nodes rendered as illuminated authority panels. Dark navy background, futuristic technical dashboard aesthetic. No text, no watermarks. Ultra clean composition, high contrast, glowing accent details. FILE: eu-biocidal-products-regulation-disinfectants-sanitisers-diagram-globalformulation.webp
